00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:25.220
about the fact that sleep
is the fundamental layer

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:27.450
of mental health, physical
health, and performance.

00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:29.908
Now one of the key things for
getting a great night's sleep

00:07:29.908 --> 00:07:32.360
every single night is to
optimize the temperature

00:07:32.360 --> 00:07:33.800
of your sleeping environment.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:37.220
Put simply, in order to fall
asleep and stay deeply asleep,

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:40.220
your body temperature needs to
drop by about 1 to 3 degrees.

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:41.970
And waking up, on
the other hand,

00:07:41.970 --> 00:07:45.470
involves a heating of your
body by about 1 to 3 degrees.

00:07:45.470 --> 00:07:48.350
With Eight sleep, you
can tune the temperature

00:07:48.350 --> 00:07:50.360
of your mattress
cover or mattress

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:53.480
to be cooler or hotter depending
on whether or not you tend

00:07:53.480 --> 00:07:54.860
to run too hot or too cold.

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:56.630
And you can even vary
it across the night

00:07:56.630 --> 00:07:59.510
so that you can access the best
deep sleep early in the night.

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:01.640
The so-called REM sleep,
rapid eye movement sleep,

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:03.890
that's more pronounced in
the later half of the night.

00:08:03.890 --> 00:08:05.390
And doing so really
get your sleep

00:08:05.390 --> 00:08:07.520
optimized not just
in terms of duration

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:10.040
but in terms of quality and
the overall architecture

00:08:10.040 --> 00:08:10.730
of your sleep.

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:13.993
This has a profound influence
on your alertness, focus, mood,

00:08:13.993 --> 00:08:16.160
and many other important
factors throughout the day.

